FORM K-1.
IN THE MATTER OF: the-labyrinth.
FILED BY: the office of the shortest petition.

OFF THE RECORD: Breadth-first search visits each open cell at most once.
OFF THE RECORD: Schedule positions represent cells in a 7 by 7 maze.
OFF THE RECORD: Predecessors reconstruct a shortest route from S to E.
OFF THE RECORD: Neighbor order is north, east, south, west.
OFF THE RECORD: Row boundaries prevent horizontal movement into another row.
OFF THE RECORD: At most 225 cells are allowed. No external input is needed.

HEREINAFTER, width SHALL MEAN 7.
HEREINAFTER, start-cell SHALL MEAN 9.
HEREINAFTER, goal-cell SHALL MEAN 41.

ARTICLE 1.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT maze IS
        "#######" PLUS
        "#S#...#" PLUS
        "#.#.#.#" PLUS
        "#...#.#" PLUS
        "###.#.#" PLUS
        "#...#E#" PLUS
        "#######".
    SHOULD width FALL SHORT OF 2 OR IN THE ALTERNATIVE width EXCEED 25, HOLD "Maze width must be between 2 and 25." IN CONTEMPT.
    SHOULD THE LENGTH OF maze EXCEED 225 OR IN THE ALTERNATIVE THE LENGTH OF maze EQUAL 0, HOLD "Maze must contain between 1 and 225 cells." IN CONTEMPT.
    SHOULD THE LENGTH OF maze NOTWITHSTANDING width DIFFER FROM 0, HOLD "Maze rows must have equal widths." IN CONTEMPT.
    SHOULD start-cell FALL SHORT OF 1 OR IN THE ALTERNATIVE start-cell EXCEED THE LENGTH OF maze, HOLD "Start cell is outside the maze." IN CONTEMPT.
    SHOULD goal-cell FALL SHORT OF 1 OR IN THE ALTERNATIVE goal-cell EXCEED THE LENGTH OF maze, HOLD "Goal cell is outside the maze." IN CONTEMPT.
    SHOULD AN EXCERPT OF maze FROM start-cell TO start-cell EQUAL "#", HOLD "Start cell is a wall." IN CONTEMPT.
    SHOULD AN EXCERPT OF maze FROM goal-cell TO goal-cell EQUAL "#", HOLD "Goal cell is a wall." IN CONTEMPT.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT predecessor IS AN EMPTY SCHEDULE.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT route IS AN EMPTY SCHEDULE.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT position IS 1.

ARTICLE 2.
    SHOULD position EXCEED THE LENGTH OF maze, REFER TO ARTICLE 3.
    ANNEX 0 TO predecessor.
    ANNEX 0 TO route.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT position IS position PLUS 1.
    REFER TO ARTICLE 2.

ARTICLE 3.
    SUBSTITUTE -1 FOR ITEM start-cell OF predecessor.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT queue IS A SCHEDULE COMPRISING start-cell.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT head IS 1.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT visited IS 0.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT directions IS A SCHEDULE COMPRISING 0 LESS width AND 1 AND width AND -1.

ARTICLE 4.
    SHOULD head EXCEED THE LENGTH OF queue, HOLD "The maze has no route to the exit." IN CONTEMPT.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT current IS THE ITEM AT head IN queue.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT visited IS visited PLUS 1.
    SHOULD current EQUAL goal-cell, REFER TO ARTICLE 6.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT direction IS 1.

ARTICLE 5.
    SHOULD direction EXCEED 4, REFER TO ARTICLE 8.
    PETITION THE OFFICE OF visit WITH current PLUS THE ITEM AT direction IN directions AND current.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT direction IS direction PLUS 1.
    REFER TO ARTICLE 5.

ARTICLE 6.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT position IS goal-cell.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT steps IS 0.

ARTICLE 7.
    SUBSTITUTE 1 FOR ITEM position OF route.
    SHOULD position EQUAL start-cell, REFER TO ARTICLE 9.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT position IS THE ITEM AT position IN predecessor.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT steps IS steps PLUS 1.
    REFER TO ARTICLE 7.

ARTICLE 8.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT head IS head PLUS 1.
    REFER TO ARTICLE 4.

ARTICLE 9.
    PROCLAIM "Shortest route: " PLUS THE TRANSCRIPT OF steps PLUS " steps.".
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT position IS 1.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT row IS "".

ARTICLE 10.
    SHOULD position EXCEED THE LENGTH OF maze, ADJOURN INDEFINITELY.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT tile IS AN EXCERPT OF maze FROM position TO position.
    SHOULD tile EQUAL ".", SHOULD THE ITEM AT position IN route EQUAL 1, LET IT BE RECORDED THAT tile IS "*".
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT row IS row PLUS tile.
    SHOULD position NOTWITHSTANDING width EQUAL 0, REFER TO ARTICLE 11.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT position IS position PLUS 1.
    REFER TO ARTICLE 10.

ARTICLE 11.
    PROCLAIM row.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT row IS "".
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT position IS position PLUS 1.
    REFER TO ARTICLE 10.

THE OFFICE OF visit, CONCERNING candidate AND parent.
    SHOULD candidate FALL SHORT OF 1, REMAND.
    SHOULD candidate EXCEED THE LENGTH OF maze, REMAND.
    SHOULD candidate EQUAL parent PLUS 1, SHOULD parent NOTWITHSTANDING width EQUAL 0, REMAND.
    SHOULD candidate EQUAL parent LESS 1, SHOULD parent NOTWITHSTANDING width EQUAL 1, REMAND.
    SHOULD THE ITEM AT candidate IN predecessor DIFFER FROM 0, REMAND.
    SHOULD AN EXCERPT OF maze FROM candidate TO candidate EQUAL "#", REMAND.
    SUBSTITUTE parent FOR ITEM candidate OF predecessor.
    ANNEX candidate TO queue.
    REMAND.
